From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Filippo Falezza <filippo.falezza@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:38:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 123/159] LOCAL: remoteproc: qcom: pas: Wait 10 s for start

Downstream waits up to 10 s for the remote to signal err_ready, while
qcom_pas_start() waits 5 s. During the SM7250 ADSP bring-up the
longer wait was used to rule out a slow start. Keep it for the nairo
branch only; it is not meant for upstream.

This patch was generated by an AI coding assistant (Claude Opus 5.5 in
Claude Code) during an interactive bring-up session on a Motorola Moto G
5G Plus (XT2075-3, "nairo"). It has not yet been reviewed line by line
by a human and needs that review before any submission.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Filippo Falezza <filippo.falezza@outlook.com>
---
 drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
index c8063cfc6131..e50bead72562 100644
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
@@ -369,7 +369,8 @@ static int qcom_pas_start(struct rproc *rproc)
 		goto unmap_carveout;
 	}
 
-	ret = qcom_q6v5_wait_for_start(&pas->q6v5, msecs_to_jiffies(5000));
+	/* LOCAL: downstream waits 10 s for err_ready; the SM7250 ADSP needs more than 5 */
+	ret = qcom_q6v5_wait_for_start(&pas->q6v5, msecs_to_jiffies(10000));
 	if (ret == -ETIMEDOUT) {
 		dev_err(pas->dev, "start timed out\n");
 		qcom_pas_shutdown(pas->pas_id);
